{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00406","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00406@rel:R25-11#602f8c77","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00406","release":"R25-11","content":"function GetCurrentFileStorageSize [SWS_PER_00406] Upstream: RS_PER_00017 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_AP_00121 , RS_AP_00127 , RS_AP_00128 , RS_AP_00129 , RS_AP_00135 , RS_AP_00137 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00159 ara::core::Result &lt; std::uint64_t &gt; GetCurrentFileStorageSize (const ara::core::InstanceSpecifier &amp;fs) noexcept; Returns the space in bytes currently occupied by a File Storage. The returned size includes all metadata and the space used for redundancy and backups. The returned size is only guaranteed to be accurate if the File Storage is not opened and no other operation on the File Storage takes place at the same time. Header-Datei #include \"ara/per/file_storage.h\" class mono Scope namespace ara::per class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit thread-safe class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td fs td The shortName path of a PortPrototype typed by a PersistencyFile StorageInterface. Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt;std::uint64_t &gt; td A Result containing the occupied space in bytes. In case of an error, it contains any of the errors defined below, or a vendor specific error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td PerErrc ::kStorageNotFound td rollback_semantics Returned if the passed InstanceSpecifier does not match any PersistencyFileStorageInterface configured for this Executable. td PerErrc ::kPhysicalStorageFailure td rollback_semantics Returned if access to the physical storage fails.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00406","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R25-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_relea